# Hermes email triage — Microsoft 365 (Outlook) inbox → intake pipeline.
#
# Every 30 minutes with a 2-hour lookback. The overlap is safe: every processed
# message is tagged with the "Hermes Triaged" category and skipped next run, and
# actionable mail dedupes downstream on internetMessageId. Noise is moved to the
# "Hermes Triage" folder (never deleted); actionable mail becomes an
# intake_submissions row that the intake worker synthesizes for human approval.
#
# Installed into root's crontab by deploy/cron/install-cron.sh. This file is the
# source of truth — DO NOT hand-edit the live crontab; edit here and re-run the
# installer so the schedule survives redeploys (it was lost once in the
# hermes-elestio → hermes-gretch migration because it lived only on the box).
*/30 * * * * cd /opt/rsg-hermes && docker compose run --rm hermes hermes --email-triage --email-provider ms365 --email-since-hours 2 >> /root/hermes-email-triage.log 2>&1
